\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The integrated runtime keeps its advantage across substrates (measured summaries): MiniGrid team cost and VMAS physics team steps (lower is better), and ALFWorld task grounding (single measured point; no convergence curve was measured). The fourth panel is the measured MAPPO baseline training curve, which plateaus at success $\approx 0.65$ --- the symbolic-peer $K{=}8$ level --- confirming the multi-agent-RL baseline is trained to convergence, so the runtime's advantage is not an artefact of an undertrained baseline.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:crosssub}{{2}{10}{The integrated runtime keeps its advantage across substrates (measured summaries): MiniGrid team cost and VMAS physics team steps (lower is better), and ALFWorld task grounding (single measured point; no convergence curve was measured). The fourth panel is the measured MAPPO baseline training curve, which plateaus at success $\approx 0.65$ --- the symbolic-peer $K{=}8$ level --- confirming the multi-agent-RL baseline is trained to convergence, so the runtime's advantage is not an artefact of an undertrained baseline}{figure.2}{}}
